.TH "REPROCTL\-HELP\-ENVIRONMENT" "7" "2026" "reproctl" "Repro Development Tools"
.SH NAME
reproctl\-help\-environment \- environment variables used by reproctl
.SH DESCRIPTION
reproctl reads the following environment variables.
Variables marked as \f[I]automatic\f[R] are set by reproctl itself and
should not be overridden.
.SH VARIABLES
.TP
\f[B]LINEAR_API_KEY\f[R]
A Linear personal API key.
Used by \f[B]reproctl wt create \-\-from\-issue\f[R] to fetch issue
metadata (branch name, title) from the Linear API.
.TP
\f[B]REPRO_WORKTREE\f[R] \f[I](automatic)\f[R]
Set to the worktree name (branch slug) inside subshells created by
\f[B]reproctl wt attach\f[R].
Empty in the main checkout.
.TP
\f[B]REPRO_WORKTREE_BRANCH\f[R] \f[I](automatic)\f[R]
Set to the full branch name inside worktree subshells created by
\f[B]reproctl wt attach\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]REPRO_WORKTREE_PATH\f[R] \f[I](automatic)\f[R]
Set to the absolute path of the worktree directory inside subshells
created by \f[B]reproctl wt attach\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]NO_COLOR\f[R]
When set to any non\-empty value, disables all colored output.
Follows the convention at \c
.UR https://no-color.org
.UE \c
\&.
Overrides terminal detection.
.TP
\f[B]REPROCTL_DEBUG\f[R]
When set to any non\-empty value, enables verbose debug output to
stderr.
Useful for troubleshooting command execution.
